WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
RF one-oh-one is a login requirement. QA FlowKit makes the workflow reviewable.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:14.000
One command installs the framework. Init selects the quick track and a manual-only preset, while doctor checks the installation.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:22.000
The requirement identifier opens a resumable run. The active phase packet tells the agent exactly what to produce next.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:30.000
The source requirement stays in the repository, together with its acceptance rule and identifier.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The agent creates analysis artifacts. Deterministic scripts verify the phase before the workflow can advance.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
A human approval point is recorded before test generation. The decision stays with the run evidence.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Now the generated feature contains an intentional defect. The required manual tag is missing.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:05.000
The gate rejects the file with a non-zero exit. The run stays on the Gherkin phase, so nothing is skipped or lost.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.000
The correction adds manual true. The same run resumes without restarting the workflow.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:22.000
The same deterministic check now passes, and the workflow moves forward to traceability.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:31.000
The traceability matrix links the source requirement, the test case, and the acceptance criterion.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:39.000
The final run status preserves each completed phase and its evidence for repository review.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Finally, validate target checks the complete repository state. No external credentials or service writes are required.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Replay the verified path from the QA FlowKit repository with npm run test E two E quick.
